1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:06,980
Today I'll show you how to design a piece of furniture made to measure for your home, straight from a hand sketch, and without any CAD knowledge.

2
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:13,090
At the end, you'll have a 3D model, workshop drawings with all dimensions, and a cut list for the timber yard.

3
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:16,960
And if you change your mind later, the agent updates everything.

4
00:00:19,271 --> 00:00:20,527
We use SOMA for this.

5
00:00:20,577 --> 00:00:24,681
It's free and open source, and you can download it at somacad.app.

6
00:00:25,381 --> 00:00:29,295
The design work is done by an AI agent, here Claude Code.

7
00:00:29,345 --> 00:00:31,431
SOMA shows you what it builds.

8
00:00:32,581 --> 00:00:33,650
Click New model.

9
00:00:35,581 --> 00:00:38,410
Then start Claude Code with the plus above the terminal.

10
00:00:39,110 --> 00:00:42,796
The first time, Claude Code asks if it may work in this folder.

11
00:00:42,846 --> 00:00:43,320
Say yes.

12
00:00:44,714 --> 00:00:47,981
My sketch is on paper, and a photo from the phone is enough.

13
00:00:48,031 --> 00:00:50,684
Click Import, and it goes into the model folder.

14
00:00:51,384 --> 00:00:52,314
Click it to open it.

15
00:00:53,014 --> 00:00:53,680
Here it is:

16
00:00:53,730 --> 00:01:00,104
a low shelf on casters, 80 centimetres wide and 60 high, with a middle shelf and two compartments.

17
00:01:00,914 --> 00:01:02,244
Then send it to the agent.

18
00:01:02,948 --> 00:01:05,642
Now describe in plain words what you want.

19
00:01:05,692 --> 00:01:06,998
No CAD terms needed.

20
00:01:10,106 --> 00:01:13,425
If something in the sketch is unclear, the agent asks.

21
00:01:13,475 --> 00:01:15,596
Here I simply take its suggestion.

22
00:01:16,906 --> 00:01:20,288
The agent looks at the sketch, plans the boards and writes the model.

23
00:01:20,338 --> 00:01:22,476
This takes a few minutes, here much faster.

24
00:01:23,420 --> 00:01:24,413
And here it is:

25
00:01:24,463 --> 00:01:26,220
a real panel construction.

26
00:01:26,270 --> 00:01:32,109
Sides, top and bottom, the middle shelf and divider, a back panel, and four casters.

27
00:01:32,809 --> 00:01:35,681
Every board is its own part in the structure tree.

28
00:01:35,731 --> 00:01:39,179
Click one in the 3D view, and SOMA shows which board it is.

29
00:01:40,429 --> 00:01:42,288
For the workshop, I need drawings.

30
00:01:42,338 --> 00:01:46,719
I simply ask for them, and the agent lays out every board with its dimensions.

31
00:01:47,419 --> 00:01:48,989
They appear in the Drawings tab:

32
00:01:49,039 --> 00:01:53,949
the views with all the main dimensions, ready to print, or to take into the workshop on a tablet.

33
00:01:57,158 --> 00:01:58,313
Next, the cut list.

34
00:01:58,363 --> 00:02:04,008
I ask for an Excel file with every board, its size and edge banding, and a shopping list.

35
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:06,721
The file lands in the model folder.

36
00:02:06,771 --> 00:02:08,598
Open it in any spreadsheet app.

37
00:02:09,348 --> 00:02:15,158
The cut list has every panel with length, width, thickness and quantity, and which edges get banding.

38
00:02:15,858 --> 00:02:20,233
The shopping list has the sheet material, the casters, screws and edge banding.

39
00:02:20,283 --> 00:02:21,908
Ready for the hardware store.

40
00:02:23,715 --> 00:02:25,303
Now, the shelf should be wider.

41
00:02:25,353 --> 00:02:27,733
The agent made the main dimensions adjustable:

42
00:02:27,783 --> 00:02:29,685
you find them in the Parameters tab.

43
00:02:30,449 --> 00:02:35,252
Drag the width from 80 to 120 centimetres, and the model updates right away.

44
00:02:35,302 --> 00:02:36,899
No agent needed for this.

45
00:02:37,949 --> 00:02:41,359
The height works the same way, and so does everything else in this list.

46
00:02:43,615 --> 00:02:44,457
One more wish:

47
00:02:44,507 --> 00:02:46,495
a door for the left compartment.

48
00:02:46,545 --> 00:02:49,234
Click Mark up, and draw right on the model:

49
00:02:49,284 --> 00:02:53,105
the outline of the door, a handle, and an arrow with a word.

50
00:02:53,805 --> 00:02:55,855
Send it to the agent, with one sentence.

51
00:02:56,555 --> 00:03:03,405
The agent builds the door with a handle and two hinges, checks that it opens freely, and brings the drawings and the cut list up to date.

52
00:03:04,556 --> 00:03:07,299
Here is the door, and the drawings show the new width too.

53
00:03:16,649 --> 00:03:18,459
And the shopping list now has the hinges.

54
00:03:20,916 --> 00:03:21,496
That's it:

55
00:03:21,546 --> 00:03:28,116
from a hand sketch to a 3D model, workshop drawings and a cut list, without drawing a single line in CAD.

56
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:30,246
Get SOMA for free at somacad.app.
